// Note that this is a client-side environment variable, so in reality it will be exposed to the browser. Do not put any sensitive information here.
// The better practice is to use server-side environment variables for sensitive information and only expose what is necessary to the client.
// TLDR: create a .env file in the server directory. and add the .env file into the .gitignore file so that it is not committed to version control. Then, use server-side code to access the sensitive information and only send what is necessary to the client.